  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: 1 mile W Obulco on Arroyo Salado</p>\r\n<p>\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The remains of a Roman bridge known locally as Puente Viejo or Puente de Ca\u00f1ete lying one mile west west of Obulco on the Arroyo Salado. The bridge may have been associated with a conjectured secondary Roman road or route between Corduba and Catulo because although unmentioned in the Antonine Itinerary, the bridge's location lies between two mentioned stations: Calpurniana and Vircao.",
